{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4558dac720390e26adeddd9fade787a9d5f8c731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ACE}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b70155a698cd22154c1d3896f11c9d09ff5bcc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69470a4eff790f95fbb1e41e800dbd9a92ea08a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101aa6d28ecd306e6bd3086306aad6ad7cfb403e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/69064985e18895b0cb09caf1ac662bb49ea116df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 60^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 67.5^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 70^{\\circ}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 75^{\\circ}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 52.5^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"463\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 